fied: 2026-09-01T22:57:03.822Z\n---\n\n2026-09-01: extracted cledger's storage layer into a new sibling package\n**`annals`** (`~/repos/evintunador/annals`, name confirmed free on npm; user\npicked it over git-ledger). Grew out of reviewing the (retired)\n`design/extension-governance` branch: rather than governing third-party\nkinds inside cledger, the store became its own layer and vocabularies\nvalidate themselves.\n\nKey decisions:\n- Envelope: schema `annals/v1`, ids `ev2-`, `conversation` renamed\n  **`stream`** ({id, seq, parent}); `actor` kept in the envelope as generic\n  attribution; content never interpreted. Third-party kinds identified by\n  `(producer.tool, kind)`; the store validates the envelope only — no\n  registry (Decision 4 of the old governance doc dissolved).\n- **Namespaces**: every op takes a `Ledger` (RepoInfo + NamespaceConfig)\n  from `openLedger()`; a namespace picks notes ref, state dir, config file,\n  cliName, and the pre-push hook invocation. cledger's namespace keeps all\n  old names (refs/notes/conversation-ledger, .cledger.json, ~/.config/\n  cledger). Separate refs are for future producers ([[project-ledger-ecosystem]]:\n  intent-recall wants its own wipeable ref per its D13).\n- ReadOptions gained `tool`, `kind: string|string[]`, `linkRel`;\n  `conversation` filter renamed `stream`.\n- cledger 0.26.0 keeps its old module paths as thin namespace-binding\n  wrappers, so turnbridge's import surface survived; `ConversationRef`\n  stays exported as an alias of `StreamRef`.\n- **No migration**: user chose wiping ev1 history over rewriting (sole\n  user). `scripts/wipe-ev1-history.sh` in conversation-ledger (dry-run\n  default) — the human runs `--execute`; agents must not.\n\nState: local branches only, nothing pushed — annals repo `main` (no remote\nyet), conversation-ledger `annals-extraction`, turnbridge `annals-cledger`.\nTests: annals 150, cledger 90, turnbridge 91, all green. cledger/turnbridge\nstay separate packages: turnbridge → cledger → annals is one-way, and\ncontext-graph/intent-recall want conversations without fabrication\nmachinery. annals CLI is minimal (sync, transport-push) by design.\n","filePath":"/Users/evintunador/.claude/projects/-Users-evintunador-repos-evintunador-conversation-ledger/memory/project-annals-extraction.md","memdirStamped":true,"originalFile":null,"structuredPatch":[],"type":"create","userModified":false},"type":"user","userType":"external","uuid":"7451d935-4164-4da7-af9d-5b02c7013388","version":"2.1.257"},"format":"claude-code-jsonl/1"},"recorded_at":"2026-09-01T22:57:31.846Z","schema":"annals/v1","stream":{"id":"claude-code:a044dbb5-5e38-4400-bb2a-97061ee33f87","seq":972}}
